{
  "_note": "Combat backgrounds (PixelLab, Logan 2026-09-28). A fight uses its location's backgrounds for its tier (the strongest enemy: boss > elite > regular), picked per fight when there's more than one. `slots` are where enemies' feet stand for 1, 2 or 3 enemies, as [x, y] fractions of the image, measured on the art so every enemy stands on the floor. `floor` is the flat ground feet may stand on ({x: [from, to], y: [from, to]} as fractions of the image, `avoid`: [x0, y0, x1, y1] spots on it that aren't, like a hole); each fight stands every enemy near its slot's x, nudged a little sideways and anywhere in that y band, on the floor (Logan, 2026-10-16: a little different each fight). `zoom` enlarges the image from its bottom edge (1 = cover the screen) to lift a floor that starts too low for the enemy row. A fight with no background here keeps the plain field and the default enemy row. `weather` draws weather over the background (PlayField): \"rain\" falls and splashes, \"snow\" floats down and settles, \"dust\" blows in gusts and lifts off the ground, all on the ground from `ground` (the y fraction of the image where the ground starts) down. `sea` (a mask image the size of the background, white = water) rolls those pixels in waves the whole fight, bigger and faster once a boss is in phase 2. `lamps` ([x, y] fractions) each cast a pool of `lamp_color` light, faint until phase 2, then pulsing like alarms down the pier (instead of the whole screen pulsing). `spray` ([x0, y0, x1, y1] fractions: the edges the water breaks over) throws spray up in phase 2. `lamp_style` \"bulbs\" makes them strung bulbs that sway and, in phase 2, stutter instead of pulsing. `rockfall` drops rocks in phase 2: from the ceiling (true) or off cliff edges ({\"from\": [[x0, x1, y], ...]}). `lamp_style` \"work\": floodlights, the bulbs' stutter without the sway. `fps_phase2` alone (no `frames_phase2`) plays `frames` at that speed in phase 2. `grade_darken` (0.7) and `grade_vignette` (0.6) set how dark phase 2 turns the image (an open pit needs its machines readable). `lava` ([{path: [[x, y], ...] from the crack down, width, pool, delay}]) erupts in phase 2, runs down its path and drains into a pool (LavaFlow). `frames` (a strip of whole-background frames, `frame_width` wide each, frame 0 = the image) animates the background at `fps`; `frames_phase2` at `fps_phase2` takes over in phase 2 (tools/sea_frames.py builds both from PixelLab-animated crops of the water).",
